WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.540 --> 00:00:02.340
Hey, this is Presh Talwalkar.

00:00:02.740 --> 00:00:05.300
A child spent $100 to get

00:00:05.300 --> 00:00:07.300
100 toy animals.

00:00:08.820 --> 00:00:11.000
The child bought at least one cat,

00:00:11.340 --> 00:00:12.300
one fish,

00:00:12.300 --> 00:00:13.420
and one bird,

00:00:13.420 --> 00:00:16.360
and did not buy
any other toys.

00:00:17.740 --> 00:00:19.640
If a cat costs $10,

00:00:19.640 --> 00:00:21.420
a fish costs $3,

00:00:21.420 --> 00:00:23.360
and a bird costs 50 cents,

00:00:23.360 --> 00:00:26.840
how many of each toy did the child buy?

00:00:27.580 --> 00:00:28.940
Can you figure it out?

00:00:29.680 --> 00:00:31.199
Give this problem a try,

00:00:31.199 --> 00:00:32.880
and when you're ready,
keep watching the

00:00:32.880 --> 00:00:34.620
video for the solution.

00:00:41.010 --> 00:00:44.550
Since the child bought 100 toys in total,

00:00:44.550 --> 00:00:47.730
we know the number of cats plus the

00:00:47.730 --> 00:00:48.899
number of fish

00:00:48.899 --> 00:00:52.350
plus the number of birds is equal to 100.

00:00:53.320 --> 00:00:56.360
Furthermore, the child spent $100

00:00:56.360 --> 00:00:59.820
in total, and we know the cost 
of each toy.

00:01:01.229 --> 00:01:03.930
This leads to the equation
that 10 times

00:01:03.930 --> 00:01:06.299
the number of cats plus 3 times the

00:01:06.299 --> 00:01:09.060
number of fish plus .5 times the

00:01:09.060 --> 00:01:11.740
number of birds is equal to 100.

00:01:14.940 --> 00:01:16.860
Let's simplify these equations.

00:01:17.140 --> 00:01:18.520
From the first equation,

00:01:18.520 --> 00:01:20.460
we'll solve for the
number of birds.

00:01:21.210 --> 00:01:24.150
This will be: the number of birds is
equal to 100

00:01:24.150 --> 00:01:25.740
minus the number of cats

00:01:25.740 --> 00:01:27.740
minus the number of fish.

00:01:29.260 --> 00:01:31.840
We can substitute that
into the second equation.

00:01:33.200 --> 00:01:35.120
We'll now simplify this

00:01:35.460 --> 00:01:37.560
and then we'll
simplify it further.

00:01:38.960 --> 00:01:40.440
We end up that 19

00:01:40.440 --> 00:01:43.289
times the number of cats
plus 5 times

00:01:43.289 --> 00:01:46.269
the number of fish is equal to 100.

00:01:47.460 --> 00:01:49.320
Let's continue from this equation.

00:01:51.200 --> 00:01:53.360
We'll solve for the number of fish.

00:01:54.620 --> 00:01:58.140
We have: the number of fish
is equal to 20 minus the

00:01:58.140 --> 00:02:01.600
number of cats times
19 over 5.

00:02:03.520 --> 00:02:05.280
This will be the key equation

00:02:05.280 --> 00:02:07.040
to deduce the answer.

00:02:09.509 --> 00:02:11.729
The variable "cats" is being multiplied

00:02:11.729 --> 00:02:13.729
by 19 over 5.

00:02:15.840 --> 00:02:17.560
Now we need the number of fish

00:02:17.560 --> 00:02:18.840
to be a whole number,

00:02:18.840 --> 00:02:20.540
and we know that
the number of cats

00:02:20.540 --> 00:02:22.170
is also a whole number.

00:02:23.520 --> 00:02:26.180
This means the number of cats has to be

00:02:26.190 --> 00:02:28.650
a multiple of 5 so that the number of

00:02:28.650 --> 00:02:30.269
fish is a whole number.

00:02:32.620 --> 00:02:34.980
Furthermore, we need the number of fish

00:02:34.980 --> 00:02:37.480
to be a number that's greater than 0.

00:02:39.060 --> 00:02:41.720
We're taking 20 minus
the number of cats

00:02:41.730 --> 00:02:43.770
times 19 over 5.

00:02:44.920 --> 00:02:47.500
So we can figure out
that the number of cats

00:02:47.500 --> 00:02:50.460
has to be less than 
100 over 19,

00:02:50.460 --> 00:02:53.760
or approximately 5.26,
so that the

00:02:53.760 --> 00:02:56.320
number of fish is greater
than 0.

00:02:58.140 --> 00:03:01.540
So we need a multiple of five
that's less than

00:03:01.540 --> 00:03:03.520
about 5.26,

00:03:03.520 --> 00:03:05.480
and we know that
the number of cats

00:03:05.480 --> 00:03:07.280
is also greater than zero.

00:03:08.100 --> 00:03:11.000
So what number is a 
multiple of 5

00:03:11.000 --> 00:03:12.440
that's greater than 0

00:03:12.440 --> 00:03:14.020
but less than 5.26?

00:03:14.020 --> 00:03:15.819
There's only one possibility,

00:03:15.819 --> 00:03:18.099
which is that the number of cats is

00:03:18.099 --> 00:03:19.699
equal to five.

00:03:19.700 --> 00:03:22.140
So we've uniquely solved for
the number of cats,

00:03:22.140 --> 00:03:23.500
and we can substitute

00:03:23.500 --> 00:03:25.150
that value to get that the number of

00:03:25.150 --> 00:03:27.090
fish has to equal 1.

00:03:29.820 --> 00:03:30.740
We now need to figure out

00:03:30.740 --> 00:03:31.800
the number of birds,

00:03:32.340 --> 00:03:34.060
but we know the total number of animals is

00:03:34.060 --> 00:03:35.060
equal to 100.

00:03:35.720 --> 00:03:38.240
So we can then say
that the number of birds

00:03:38.240 --> 00:03:40.239
is equal to 94,

00:03:40.600 --> 00:03:43.690
and this is the unique solution
to this problem.

00:03:45.600 --> 00:03:46.900
Did you figure it out?

